The election resulted in a major political realignment, effectively ending the Communist Party's brief period of governance. The Progressive Party of Okaiken saw a massive victory, gaining 70 seats to become the largest party in the House of Commoners. However, at 201 seats, they fell 37 seats short of the 238 needed for an outright majority.

The Sanese Communist Party, led by incumbent Prime Minister Sho Aoyagi, suffered a significant backlash from voters, losing 48 seats and its position as the largest party. The LDP, under Sadakazu Tanizaki, failed to recover from its 2016 losses, dropping another 4 seats to remain in third place, a sign of its continued struggle for relevance.

The most dramatic collapse was that of the Okaiken Socialist Party, which was reduced from 46 seats to just 2, becoming the smallest party in the house and losing its official party status.

Smaller parties saw modest to significant gains. The New Komeito Party gained 5 seats, the Social Democratic Party gained 11, and the newly-rebranded Okaiken Innovation Party (formerly "Kei Yamada and Friends") secured 10 additional seats, bringing its total to 12.

Following the election, Honda Shigetsuma was invited by the Emperor to form a government. After brief negotiations, he successfully formed a PPO minority government, securing confidence and supply agreements from the Social Democratic Party and the New Komeito Party in exchange for policy concessions.

===Notable losses===
*[[Oizumi Yu]] (OSP), the long-serving leader of the Okaiken Socialist Party, lost his own seat in a stunning upset, precipitating his party's near-total collapse.

===Notable wins===
*All other major party leaders—[[Honda Shigetsuma]] (PPO), [[Sho Aoyagi]] (SCP), [[Sadakazu Tanizaki]] (LDP), [[Okada Junichiro]] (NKP), [[Shimane Yoshida]] (SDP), and [[Kei Yamada]] (OIP)—successfully defended their respective seats.
